WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.540
Here's how to make two macros in PadForge: a button chord that sends a shortcut,

2
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.650
and a button that types a message.

3
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.870
You're hearing a generated voice.

4
00:00:11.275 --> 00:00:14.885
Open the controller, go to the Macros tab, and click Add.

5
00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.200
Name it Task Manager.

6
00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:23.711
Under Trigger, open Add from List, and pick Gamepad Left Shoulder.

7
00:00:24.121 --> 00:00:26.161
Open it again, and add Gamepad Right Shoulder.

8
00:00:26.201 --> 00:00:28.911
Holding both together is the chord.

9
00:00:31.136 --> 00:00:33.306
Add an action, and make it a Key Press.

10
00:00:33.916 --> 00:00:38.366
In Key Combo, type Control, Shift and Escape, each in curly braces.

11
00:00:38.896 --> 00:00:40.966
That shortcut opens Task Manager.

12
00:00:44.173 --> 00:00:46.223
Click Add again for a second macro.

13
00:00:46.693 --> 00:00:49.463
Name it Good Game, and give it Gamepad D-Pad Up.

14
00:00:52.426 --> 00:00:54.316
Its action is a Text Block.

15
00:00:54.646 --> 00:00:55.636
Type the message here.

16
00:00:56.801 --> 00:01:00.641
Press up on the pad, and PadForge types it out, letter by letter.

17
00:01:00.681 --> 00:01:03.051
Both macros save as you go.

18
00:01:05.225 --> 00:01:07.755
Find more guides at padforge.org.
